<row>
  <text size=34%>
    ## Column widths: `size`

    In a `<row>` every part takes an equal share of the width.
    `size=34%` makes this one narrower, here for a short note next to wider code. `size=2` would be a weight: twice as wide.
  </text>
  <code lang=typescript>
    <frame>
      const columns = { text: "34%", code: "the rest" };
    </frame>
    <frame>
      const columns = { text: "34%", code: "the rest", gap: "4vmin" };
    </frame>
  </code>
</row>
